146
00:06:49,660 --> 00:06:52,740
This first phrase is a way of expressing something.

147
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:55,700
So we're going to give you a formula.

148
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:56,290
The first word is leading.

149
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:58,910
So leading mobile phone manufacturers.

150
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:03,880
So when we use the word leading, we're saying that it's leading an industry.

151
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:08,050
That means the most important manufacturers in a kind of industry.

152
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,200
Right.

153
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:09,390
So it's one of the biggest.

154
00:07:10,200 --> 00:07:11,200
It's one of the best.

155
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:17,070
And if we want to change the noun, we can say for example, the leading car manufacturer.

156
00:07:17,730 --> 00:07:18,270
Exactly.

157
00:07:18,590 --> 00:07:21,470
So in Japan, I wonder who the leading car manufacturer is.

158
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:21,910
Is it Toyota?

159
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,520
Toyota.

160
00:07:23,570 --> 00:07:26,050
And we could also say that about clothing.

161
00:07:26,710 --> 00:07:32,690
The leading clothing manufacturer in America is, I have no idea, cotton maybe?

162
00:07:33,190 --> 00:07:33,990
Cotton, right.

163
00:07:34,410 --> 00:07:36,250
So you can use many other nouns.

164
00:07:36,330 --> 00:07:45,590
And well, if you want to drop the manufacturers, you can say the leading brand in cosmetics or the leading supplier of medical equipment.

165
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:52,430
So this means the person or the company that's the most important in an industry.

166
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:54,160
Right.

167
00:07:54,160 --> 00:08:00,240
So going back to one of the features of the mobile phone, we talked about the built in camera.

168
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:00,810
Now this structure is interesting.

169
00:08:01,520 --> 00:08:01,990
Built in.

170
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:07,340
Well, we can say that things are built in when they are a part of something else.

171
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:11,700
For example, a built in camera is a part of a phone.

172
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:15,020
It's not a camera and a phone, two different devices.

173
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:15,980
They're put together.

174
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:18,380
We can also say this about cabinets.

175
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:24,100
You know, you can buy cabinets and you can put them in your house and keep things in them.

176
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,260
But we often have built ins.

177
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:28,060
That means that they're stuck on the wall.

178
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,080
You can't take them away.

179
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,440
Right.

180
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:32,640
So those are called built ins because they're part of the wall.

181
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:34,560
So built in camera is a part of the phone.

182
00:08:34,580 --> 00:08:34,720
Right.

183
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:39,200
So you can pretty much use this structure with two products that are combined as one.

184
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:49,760
For example, the cabinets that Catherine mentioned, or if your refrigerator has a television incorporated, right, you can say this refrigerator comes with a built in television.

185
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:54,100
Or very common is the laptop with built in speakers.

186
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:58,300
So that means we don't have to bring speakers with us every time we want to use the laptop.

187
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:00,480
There's small speakers inside the computer.

188
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,080
Right.

189
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,080
